{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1470458-why-is-nippon-frightened-of-novas","id":1470458,"title":"Why is Nippon Frightened of Novas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-14T12:04:09-08:00","id":1470458,"title":"Why is Nippon Frightened of Novas?","content":"Nippon devloped a test to detect the potential for Nova (or unknown to them, Psionic) potential, and from this eventually sprang the Superior treatment. <br /> <br /> But... It strikes me that of all the nations, Nippon should have the most positive attitude towards Novas, especially since they canonically developed tests that allowed them to determine if a Nova would fall to madness. Because of this, Up until 2104, Nippon's government worked with dozens of <i>sane</i> novas, who played an immense role in ensuring the survival of the nation--and then, with the fall of the quantum barrier, died attempted to protect Earth from their maddened counterparts. <br /> <br /> So given the existence of tests to determine a Nova's sanity, and a test for Nova potential, why woudln't Nippon try to arrange for at least a few Nova eruptions? A superior is a powerful asset, but even so, Nova's, especially megaintellitent ones, had a great deal to offer Nippon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T12:36:02-08:00","id":1470462,"title":"","content":"The test in TC is not about \u201cturning mad\u201d, it\u2019s about being capable of erupt and be dedicated to the country.<br /> <br /> I have the feeling that, in TC, Aberrant War stories are told by the humans only and that not all the things that are narrated are really the way they narrated. I mean, novas did a lot of bad things, and killed many, but the war was fought by humans, Aberrants were not a team fighting a war, they were a bunch of individuals (as powerful as nations, to be fair) fighting for their lives and what they believed were their rights.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Nihon didn\u2019t suffer from the war as the rest of the world did, but they know that once they have novas, they would be targeted by all other nations. The tests can\u2019t detect capacity of going mad, only if they are capable of erupt and if they follow a strict psychological profile. Eruptions can be dangerous, even more living in closed archeologists, so just let a nova erupt may be risky. So they control the eruptions and still keep some of the nova advantages in the form of superiors.<br /> <br /> Thats not a bad deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T13:51:34-08:00","id":1470468,"title":"","content":"Well, I got the impression that Nippon is a nation that is paranoid about everything. It's citizens are afraid to go outside, for instance. The risk of a Nova you can't control just is not worth the benefits of a Nova you can, in their view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T14:23:38-08:00","id":1470474,"title":"","content":"Nippon doesn't really fear Nova's, considering a lot of their tech is due to them having access to mega-intelligence Nova's that didn't go nutso. They just control them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T15:48:32-08:00","id":1470482,"title":"","content":"Yeah--I mean, the Trinity core book mentions that by 2049, they had some method of testing novas for <i>stability</i>. not just potential, but whether or not a nova would go insane. So, it would seem to make sense to allow other novas to erupt and then test them. The later genetic test was just for whether or not you had nova potential. <br /> <br /> Here's the text:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">By 2049, tests allowed Nihonjin<br /> scientists to discover which novas were most likely<br /> to become dangerously unstable. Since there was no<br /> way to prevent or reverse this growing madness, the<br /> Nihonjin government attempted to exile or secretly<br /> execute any nova who failed these tests.<br /> When it closed its borders in 2053, the Nihonjin<br /> government allowed more than three dozen sane and<br /> loyal novas to remain. Tests revealed that these novas<br /> would not become dangerously insane,</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now of course what the tests were and how foolproof they were is left open. It's possible that say, they had a 10 percent &quot;fail&quot; rate and after a few examples of &quot;and our sane nova is now talking in third person.&quot; They may have decided to not risk it, though that does seem odd, since well, almost three dozen supergenius novas would seem to open up a lot of options for coming up with something. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T16:25:03-08:00","id":1470486,"title":"","content":"In the original edition I believe that the &quot;sane&quot; Novas were the ones who had the &quot;Taint Resistant&quot; merit you could get from the Player's Guide. There might be something similar that you could buy in the new edition, like an Edge you would have available and need to choose if you were playing a Nova with a hypothetical &quot;Nippon Affiliated&quot; Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T21:25:15-08:00","id":1470500,"title":"","content":"Alternately, different novas are built using different subgenres, and their tests detect the ones built using the horror rules. You could also say that not everyone has the same inherent potential; some NPC novas may not be able to achieve high Quantum scores, and therefore wouldn't gain Transcendence for hitting those benchmarks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T22:38:28-08:00","id":1470502,"title":"","content":"There's that. I mean, another possibility is that we know how to avoid going nuts--doin't run for power. Even novas using chrysalis can avoid insanity and pay down their flux--if they're willing to. <br /> <br /> Which might be the reason Nippon hasn't tried to create new novas. IT's a test that only works when you have enough of a psychological baseline to see if the person is going to run for power at any cost, but it's not something that can be tested for before a nova erupts. And not being complete sociopaths, Nippon decided: &quot;let's not produce people when we will have to murder a not insubstantial percentage of them.&quot;<br /> <br /> It might also explain why nobody really noticed their novas--they were probably people who went wide rather than shot ahead for power, with low quantum levels--which made them very useful for Japan, but not super obvious.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}